{"author":{"id":"2eecc7d99b502c158aacb0868dca9358610edc02724d21fe49b0196402d3364e"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1787774737,"nonce":"TO77LAPFR4h5hMwHys98TtpSe7Q=","title":"fix(artifacts): index every uploaded artifact — the decorators dropped the harvest (98ea804)","message":"\u003e Imported from pull request #78 (MERGED)\n\u003e Branch: `fix/dogfood-artifacts-never-indexed` → `main`\n\u003e Created: 2026-07-25T18:04:35Z · Merged: 2026-07-25T18:14:21Z\n\nCloses git-bug `98ea804`.\n\nThe hypothesised annotation/scheduler race was real but **already fixed on `main`** by `2fb0b9b` (2026-07-18), which withholds the Succeeded verdict while the egress sidecar is still running. That fix shipped with **no test**.\n\nWhat still lost the index write — **on every run, on every backend**:\n\n`Executor::artifacts` has an empty trait default, and **neither executor decorator forwarded it**. Production wires `CloneEnrichingExecutor(SecretInjectingExecutor(K8sExecutor))` and the scheduler asks the *outermost* object. So:\n\n1. step exits 0 → sidecar harvests, uploads blobs, patches the `scarab.io/artifacts` annotation, releases the barrier\n2. `poll` → Succeeded; scheduler calls `executor.artifacts(handle)`\n3. that lands on `CloneEnrichingExecutor`'s **inherited default** → `Ok(vec![])`\n4. `if !artifacts.is_empty()` → `put_artifacts` skipped; step finalized; never polled again\n5. `GET /v1/runs/{id}/artifacts` → `[]` forever, with blobs *and* annotation both present\n\nExactly the dogfood evidence. Both decorators already carry comments about this forward-or-drop hazard for `results` / `log_stream` / services — `artifacts` was simply missed.\n\n- **Forward `artifacts()`** in both decorators, and document the contract on the port: a decorator must forward; a backend must not report an unsettled harvest as an empty one.\n- **A harvest error is now `DriveErr::Transient`** instead of a swallowed `eprintln!`. That closes a residual race: blobs uploaded → annotation patch fails on an apiserver blip → barrier released anyway → Succeeded with nothing indexed. Now the barrier stays closed, Succeeded stays withheld, and the next poll re-harvests idempotently (same object keys; the annotation guard makes a completed harvest once-only). Bounded by the existing step-timeout backstop, so a permanently broken harvest settles as Timeout — it never reports success having lost the index. No sleeps, no retry loop.\n- `settled_state()` / `artifact_harvest_owed()` extracted as pure Pod-derived functions so the barrier rules are testable without a cluster.\n\nBoth acceptance tests fail before the fix with the ticket's exact symptom — **independently reproduced** by reverting only the two decorator files to `main`:\n`assertion failed: the uploaded artifact must be indexed, not silently dropped: []  left: 0  right: 1`\nRestored, all 5 pass.\n\n- `published_artifacts_are_indexed_through_the_decorated_executor_stack` — real router + real `Scheduler` + the real decorator chain. A test against the bare backend would have passed throughout, which is why it composes the stack.\n- `published_artifacts_are_durably_indexed_in_postgres` — same invariant against real PG, keyed per attempt (ADR-0056).\n- Two barrier-rule tests, which finally give `2fb0b9b` coverage.\n\nIntegrated with the other three dogfood branches: **597 passed, 21 ignored** with `SCARAB_TEST_REQUIRE_PG=1`.\n\nOn k8s a **failed** attempt's artifacts are never harvested at all — `drive_workspace` gates the harvest on `exit == 0`, so the scheduler's `ExecState::Failed` harvest branch (\"often THE evidence\") is dead code on that backend, contradicting ADR-0056. Fixing it also requires withholding the `Failed{class: Step}` verdict until settle completes, or it re-introduces uploaded-but-unindexed for failures. A design call, not a silent add-on.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)","files":null}]}